WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.590
We are all insecure.

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.750
Some a little more than others.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.280
Some a little less.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:13.990
And perhaps some are just better at working
around it, while others wear it on their sleeves.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.350
Nonetheless, we are all insecure.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:23.910
We’re all insecure about who we are, because
none of us truly know who or what that is.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:30.750
We’re all insecure about our achievements
or lack there of, because we’re wired to

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.450
never feel like enough is ever enough.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:41.390
And we’re all insecure about life itself,
because it looms over us with its apathetic

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:46.550
bravado, mocking our ignorance to its mystery.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:53.690
Arguably, insecurity is in us all, fully included
with the human condition.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:00.420
From an evolutionary standpoint, the state
of insecurity is likely to be essential.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:07.560
It is what has kept us on our toes throughout
history, forcing us to remain on high alert,

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:14.080
safe from our environmental conditions and
those who seek to defeat us.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:20.330
And it is also, to some degree, at the root
of the motivation to progress and achieve

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.790
success in life.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:28.820
To attempt to impact the world and acquire
a sense of importance.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:37.020
But then how can we reduce our sense of insecurity
if it is so essentially a part of us?

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:43.520
On one hand, you are a part of the collective
humanity, and the quality of your life experience

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:49.390
is partially based on your ability to contribute
to its forward movement.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:55.619
To feel like you have a sense of contribution
outside of yourself.

00:01:55.619 --> 00:02:02.070
But simultaneously, you are a uniquely complex
being with a meaningful, individual experience

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:08.869
of life that you should enjoy and appreciate,
without it getting reduced by a constant need

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:13.810
to influence, impress, or prove something.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:18.300
And this is what we must understand and gain
agency over.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.430
That as humans, we have a conflict in our
nature.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:26.970
Our experience of life is both individual
and collective.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:33.730
But we can and should reduce the affects of
this conflict by becoming aware of it and

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:42.450
setting limitations for how much we let it
impose a sense of insecurity into our life.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.739
Use insecurity to your advantage.

00:02:45.739 --> 00:02:48.890
Use it to light the flame within you.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:56.780
To facilitate self-discipline and proficiency,
so you can do cool things and impact the world

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.180
in positive ways.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:05.510
So you can feel involved, fulfilled, and plugged
in to the collective.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:12.910
Use insecurity as this fuel, but know and
remind yourself that that’s all it is.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:18.459
That as an individual, you’re obligation
in life is not solely to contribute to the

00:03:18.459 --> 00:03:21.130
evolution of the collective.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:29.069
But that as a self-aware, conscious individual,
it is also to appreciate your own existence.

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:35.409
To appreciation that against all odds, you
get to experience the phenomenon of life as

00:03:35.409 --> 00:03:37.659
your unique self.

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:42.380
And you need nothing beyond that to revel
in the beauty of it all.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:49.959
To extend beyond the foolishness of draining
insecurity and self-doubt.

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:56.600
Contribute and find fulfillment in helping
humanity push the massive boulder of evolution

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.220
forward.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:03.849
But don’t forget that we don’t even know
where we are pushing it or why we are pushing

00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:05.500
it in the first place.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:09.880
And that we are all a little insecure about
that.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:40.610
But perhaps by simply realizing this, you
might just feel a little less insecure.

